e Olympic gold medal in this class in a hard-fought 2-1 victory over Azerbaijan’s Qazyumov, the world number three and twice Olympic bronze medalist (96kg), an opponent he had lost to just a month prior to the 2016 Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Not only did Snyder became the youngest Olympic wrestling champion in United States history (age 21) just one year after becoming his nation’s youngest World champion, his gold was the USA’s only men’s wrestling medal at the Rio Games, and the sixth in Olympic history for his nation in this weight class. In his semi-final, Snyder defeated world number six Georgia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/134096"} "Elizbar Odikadze"] " 9-4. Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/135666"} "Albert Saritov"] " and Uzbekistan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/136630"} "Magomed Ibragimov"] " won the bronze medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136404"} "Kyle Snyder"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "21"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "28"] [:td {} "8"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gol